# What this repository deliberately DOES commit, so nobody adds a rule for it
# later: covmap/ holds the behaviour rubric, its run records and the rendered
# page, all reviewed in a diff; ledger/ holds the issue records and their
# rendered page; internal/cli/assets/cs-campaign-member.bin is a text
# placeholder the build replaces, and `create` refuses to install one.
#
# Campaign material is not ignored either, because none belongs here at all:
# profiles, missions, briefs and archives live in a workspace outside this
# checkout (CONTRIBUTING.md).

# Go build output
/bin/

# goreleaser release artifacts
/dist/

# Local credentials and env config
/.env
*.key

# Private terms scripts/lint-oss.py scans for. The file names exactly what this
# project considers private, so committing it would publish the list itself.
/.leakterms

# Scratch space for a run in progress, and anything an operator archived here
# by mistake. Archives belong outside the checkout.
/.tmp/
/archives/
/dispatch-viewer/out/

# The covmap run buffer: every `go test` appends to it, and `make covmap` folds
# it into the tracked covmap/results.json. Committing the buffer would commit
# the same records twice.
/covmap/runs.local.jsonl

# Go coverage data. Every test target writes a tier directory here; the merged
# profile and the report are derived from them. The baseline (.coverage-baseline)
# is committed on purpose — it is what makes a lost suite reviewable.
/.coverage/

# Editor state
/.vscode/

# A stray build of the guest binary at the root. The embed placeholder lives at
# internal/cli/assets/cs-campaign-member.bin and must stay the only copy.
/cs-campaign-member
